speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, my motion is presented as a matter of urgent and pressing necessity and national concern under Standing Order 43. Quite frankly, I believe it is deserving of unanimous support by all members of this House. Whereas steps have been made to import or introduce into Canada the film "The Three Faces of Jesus"; whereas this is Holy Week and all Christian Canadians and good, decent-thinking Canadians of various other religious faiths are concerned with the import, introduction and showing of such a distorted and ill-conceived film in Canada; and whereas there has been a general lowering of the appreciation of the fundamental principles and ideals of Christianity and this film will result in greater depreciation of these basic principles and ideals and the general morals of society in Canada under the guise of freedom, liberty, and permissiveness; and whereas various other nations have already taken steps not to allow the said film in their country; therefore, I

would move, seconded by the hon. member for Champlain (Mr. Matte):
(1)	That this House go on record as strongly opposing the importation and/or introduction into Canada and showing of the film "The Three Faces of Jesus";
(2)	That the Prime Minister, Secretary of State, Minister of Justice, Solicitor General and the Minister of National Revenue use their good offices, in conjunction with the appropriate provincial officials, to cause this film not to be imported, introduced or shown in Canada;
(3)	That such other steps as it may deem necessary be taken by the governor general in council-that is, the cabinet-or any of its members to carry out the purport of this motion;
(4)	That this motion be acted upon immediately during this Holy Week period prior to Good Friday and Easter Sunday, the saddest and most joyous days in the Christian year.
